[89 0 0 -89 0 0] /Helvetica-Bold/Helvetica-BoldWE sf
0 (Abstract)false 0 83 0 0 0 0 360 0 313 1503 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Helvetica/HelveticaWE sf
0 (HTML+ is a simple SGML based format for wide-area hypertext documents, for use within the World)false 0 53 0 0 0 0 2482 0 313 1641 sb
0 (Wide Web. Unlike desktop publishing formats, HTML+ captures the logical intent of authors. This)false 0 53 0 0 0 0 2397 0 313 1708 sb
0 (simplifies the task of writing documents, and permits them to be effectively rendered on a wide range)false 0 53 0 0 0 0 2498 0 313 1775 sb
0 (of display types as well as the printed page.)false 0 53 0 0 0 0 1084 0 313 1842 sb
0 (HTML+ represents a substantial improvement over the existing format: HTML, offering nested lists,)false 0 53 0 0 0 0 2451 0 313 1942 sb
0 (figures, embedded data in foreign formats for equations etc, tables with support for titles and column)false 0 53 0 0 0 0 2487 0 313 2009 sb
0 (headings, change bars, entry forms for querying and updating information sources and for use as)false 0 53 0 0 0 0 2408 0 313 2076 sb
0 (questionaires for mailing. This document specifies the HTML+ format with guidelines on how it)false 0 53 0 0 0 0 2330 0 313 2143 sb
0 (should be rendered by browsers.)false 0 53 0 0 0 0 816 0 313 2210 sb
[89 0 0 -89 0 0] /Helvetica-Bold/Helvetica-BoldWE sf
0 (Introduction)false 0 83 0 0 0 0 518 0 313 2383 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Times-Roman/Times-RomanWE sf
0 (The World Wide Web is a wide area client-server architecture for retrieving hypermedia documents across the)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2491 0 313 2523 sb
0 (Internet. It also supports a means for searching remote information sources, for example bibliographies, phone)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2492 0 313 2590 sb
0 (directories and instruction manuals. There are three main ingredients:)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 1569 0 313 2657 sb
0 (a\051)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 44 0 413 2757 sb
0 (Universal naming scheme for documents. The universal resource location syntax specifies)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2033 0 513 2757 sb
0 (documents in terms of the protocol to be used to retrieve them, their Internet host and path name.)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2188 0 513 2824 sb
0 (A format for location independent lifetime identifiers is currently being defined by working)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2068 0 513 2891 sb
0 (groups of the IETF. A network protocol will allow universal resource numbers \050URNs\051 to be)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2088 0 513 2958 sb
0 (resolved to the URL for the nearest available copy.)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 1149 0 513 3025 sb
0 (b\051)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 47 0 413 3125 sb
0 (Use of available protocols for retrieving documents over the network, including FTP, NNTP,)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2095 0 513 3125 sb
0 (WAIS, Gopher, and HTTP. The latter is designed specifically for use with the World Wide Web,)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2182 0 513 3192 sb
0 (and combines efficiency with an ability to flexibly exchange information between clients and)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2104 0 513 3259 sb
0 (servers.)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 174 0 513 3326 sb
0 (c\051)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 44 0 413 3426 sb
0 (A document format supporting hypertext links based on URLs and URNs which can specify)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2074 0 513 3426 sb
0 (documents anywhere in the Internet. HTML+ is designed for rendering on a wide variety of)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2065 0 513 3493 sb
0 (different display types and platforms.)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 845 0 513 3560 sb
0 (Information browsers can display information in a wide variety of formats, e.g. plain text, rich text in the)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2367 0 313 3660 sb
0 (HTML+ format, images in the GIF and JPEG formats, MPEG movies, and MIME documents. The hypertext)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2447 0 313 3727 sb
0 (format has a special significance as it allows users to navigate from one document to the next at the click of a)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2467 0 313 3794 sb
0 (button. It provides the basis for menus, cross references, either within a document or to other documents,)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2367 0 313 3861 sb
