0 (Logical markup also preserves essential distinctions that are often lost by lower level procedural formats,)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2374 0 313 341 sb
0 (making it easier to carry out operations like indexing, and conversion into other document formats.)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2233 0 313 408 sb
0 (Practical experience has shown that people often make mistakes when they have to type in the markup for)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2388 0 313 508 sb
0 (themselves. As a result, most browsers are tolerant of bad markup. This problem is being minimised by)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2331 0 313 575 sb
0 (keeping the format as simple as possible and encouraging the development of WYSIWYG editors.)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2220 0 313 642 sb
[111 0 0 -111 0 0] /Helvetica-Bold/Helvetica-BoldWE sf
0 (The HTML+ Document Format)false 0 104 0 0 0 0 1585 0 313 810 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Times-Roman/Times-RomanWE sf
0 (The following sections go through the various features of the format with suggestions as to how browsers)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2377 0 313 975 sb
0 (should render them. The DTD for HTML+ is given in Appendix I.)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 1493 0 313 1042 sb
[67 0 0 -67 0 0] /Helvetica-Bold/Helvetica-BoldWE sf
0 (Parsing HTML+ Documents)false 0 63 0 0 0 0 873 0 313 1138 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Times-Roman/Times-RomanWE sf
0 (By default, HTML+ documents are made up of 8-bit characters in the ISO 8859 Latin-1 character set. In)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2350 0 313 1253 sb
0 (future, 16 bit character sets may be used to cover a wider range of languages. The HTTP network protocol uses)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2504 0 313 1320 sb
0 (the MIME  standard \050RFC 1341\051 to specify the document type and the character set. It is assumed that the)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2384 0 313 1387 sb
0 (chosen character set includes the printable 7 bit US ASCII characters as a subset.)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 1827 0 313 1454 sb
0 (The DTD specifies the syntax of the document structure, in particular, which tags are permitted in any given)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2442 0 313 1554 sb
0 (context. Certain tags are only permitted at the start of the document. Tags and attribute names are case)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2310 0 313 1621 sb
0 (insensitive, thus <TITLE> is equivalent to <title>. End tags may be minimised to </> instead of say </title>.)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2450 0 313 1688 sb
0 (In general, SGML entity definitions are used to represent characters which would otherwise be confused with)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2467 0 313 1788 sb
0 (markup elements:)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 403 0 313 1855 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Courier/CourierWE sf
0 (&)false 0 45 0 0 0 0 34 0 413 1960 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Times-Roman/Times-RomanWE sf
0 (is represented by)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 382 0 713 1955 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Courier/CourierWE sf
0 (&amp;)false 0 45 0 0 0 0 170 0 1313 1960 sb
0 (<)false 0 45 0 0 0 0 34 0 413 2060 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Times-Roman/Times-RomanWE sf
0 (is represented by)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 382 0 713 2055 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Courier/CourierWE sf
0 (&lt;)false 0 45 0 0 0 0 136 0 1313 2060 sb
0 (>)false 0 45 0 0 0 0 34 0 413 2160 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Times-Roman/Times-RomanWE sf
0 (is represented by)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 382 0 713 2155 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Courier/CourierWE sf
0 (&gt;)false 0 45 0 0 0 0 136 0 1313 2160 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Times-Roman/Times-RomanWE sf
0 (Such entity definitions should be used in all places except within attribute values for tags \050tag names and)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2363 0 313 2255 sb
0 (attribute names cannot contain these particular characters\051. Entity definitions can also be used for special)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2368 0 313 2322 sb
0 (characters, e.g. "&eacute;" for a small e with an accute accent. The full list is given in Appendix II. Additional)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2491 0 313 2389 sb
0 (entities may be defined within documents using the SGML entity declaration tag !ENTITY, e.g.)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2163 0 313 2456 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Courier/CourierWE sf
0 (<!ENTITY % sgml "Standardised General Markup Language">)false 0 45 0 0 0 0 1870 0 413 2552 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Times-Roman/Times-RomanWE sf
0 (The browser will then insert the full form whenever it comes across "&sgml;".)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 1770 0 313 2645 sb
0 (Repeated white space characters such as space, tab, carriage return, line feed and form feed are ignored except)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2487 0 313 2745 sb
0 (within preformatted text, i.e. it doesn't matter which white space characters you use or how many of them you)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2477 0 313 2812 sb
0 (put between words, or before or after markup elements, the effect is the same as a single space character.)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2365 0 313 2879 sb
0 (It is recommended that HTML+ documents start with the following external identifier, indicating that the)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2377 0 313 2979 sb
0 (document conforms to the HTML+ DTD. This will ensure that other SGML parsers can process HTML+)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2364 0 313 3046 sb
0 (documents, without needing to include the DTD with each document.)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 1566 0 313 3113 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Courier/CourierWE sf
0 (<!DOCTYPE htmlplus PUBLIC "-//Internet/RFC xxxx//EN">)false 0 45 0 0 0 0 1802 0 413 3209 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Times-Roman/Times-RomanWE sf
0 (HTML+ departs slightly from pure presentation independence by allowing authors to specify rendering hints,)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2466 0 313 3302 sb
0 (e.g. to use a bold font for a given type of emphasis. This step was taken to give authors greater control over the)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2501 0 313 3369 sb
0 (final appearence, and is based upon practical experience with the earlier HTML format. In addition, attribute)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2451 0 313 3436 sb
0 (values are used to distinguish different subcategories of markup, rather than adding extra tags. New logical)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2412 0 313 3503 sb
0 (categories of emphasis etc. can be added in future without needing to change existing browsers. These)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2303 0 313 3570 sb
0 (decisions have made it practical to restrict HTML+ to a very small set of tags.)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 1760 0 313 3637 sb
[67 0 0 -67 0 0] /Helvetica-Bold/Helvetica-BoldWE sf
0 (Backwards Compatibility with HTML)false 0 63 0 0 0 0 1154 0 313 3733 sb
[56 0 0 -56 0 0] /Times-Roman/Times-RomanWE sf
0 (The format is designed to be largely compatible with the earlier format HTML, and HTML+ browsers will be)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2471 0 313 3848 sb
0 (able to display documents in the HTML format with little extra cost. Suggestions on how to map HTML)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 2351 0 313 3915 sb
0 (elements to HTML+ are given in Appendix III.)false 0 50 0 0 0 0 1063 0 313 3982 sb
